Basic information (basic_info): demographics and chief complaint, including age, gender, occupation, visit time and principal symptoms. Be concise and highlight the main concern.
Example: Patient, male, 62 years old, presents with intermittent left flank discomfort for more than four months.

Present illness (present_illness): onset, symptoms, course, prior diagnosis and treatment, and response, recorded chronologically and logically.
Example: Four months ago the patient developed left flank pain without an obvious trigger. The pain is intermittent, tolerable and non-radiating, without clear aggravation or relief from activity or rest. No hematuria, urinary irritation, dysuria, fever, chills, nausea or vomiting. Two weeks ago CT at a local hospital in Zhejiang suggested bilateral renal stones. Admission was advised but declined, without further treatment. At our hospital WBC was 4.63 x 10^9/L, Hb 143 g/L and PLT 202 x 10^9/L. Urine WBC was 29.4 cells/ul, bacteria 127.8/ul, nitrite negative and urine culture negative. Creatinine was 147 umol/L and BUN 7.4 mmol/L. CT showed lumbar scoliosis and lordosis, posterior/superior displacement of both kidneys, normal size and morphology, and bilateral renal calculi with density 1200 HU. Admission was proposed for bilateral renal stones.

Past history (past_history): relevant illnesses, surgery, trauma, allergy, personal and family history.
Example:
1. Chronic illness: hypertension for six years, intermittently treated with oral telmisartan with acceptable control. Denies diabetes, heart disease and other chronic illnesses.
2. Surgery, trauma and transfusion: fall from height 55 years ago at age seven, causing thoracic and spinal deformity. Two lumbar abscesses 30 years ago resolved after drainage. Extracorporeal shockwave treatment for bilateral renal stones ten years ago, details unknown and no subsequent review. Cerebral hemorrhage two years ago treated conservatively. Denies transfusion.
3. Marriage, reproductive and family history: married at 22, one son, family healthy.
4. Tobacco, alcohol and addictive substances: denies use.
5. Vaccination: none in the past year.
6. Allergy: denies allergy.
7. Personal history: retired company employee living long-term in Wenzhou, Zhejiang, without toxic or radiation exposure or residence in epidemic areas.

Physical examination (physical_exam): objectively describe actual vital signs and system findings.
Example: Height 186 cm, weight 63.8 kg, temperature 36.6 C, pulse 65/min, respiration 18/min, BP 170/102 mmHg. Alert and in fair condition. No jaundice or palpable superficial lymphadenopathy. No notable heart/lung findings. Abdomen soft without tenderness or rebound, liver/spleen not palpable. Severe spinal kyphosis and scoliosis. No renal-angle tenderness, ureteral tenderness or palpable bladder. Patient declined digital rectal examination. No lower-limb edema or pathological reflexes.

Auxiliary examination (aux_exam): objective laboratory and imaging data, with timing and numerical values.
Example: Today at our hospital WBC 4.63 x 10^9/L, Hb 143 g/L, PLT 202 x 10^9/L. Outside urinalysis: WBC 29.4 cells/ul, bacteria 127.8/ul, nitrite negative. Urine culture negative two weeks earlier at the local Zhejiang hospital. Creatinine 147 umol/L, BUN 7.4 mmol/L. CT: lumbar scoliosis/lordosis, both kidneys displaced posteriorly and superiorly, normal size/morphology, bilateral stones with density 1200 HU. Left stone approximately 2.7 x 3.6 cm and right stone approximately 1.2 x 1.0 cm.
